{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Bare</b> — a term of uncovering, as in 'and a wall bare a shield' (2 Samuel 1:21)." "And the word תעור is from the nif'al binyan, from a different root, on the pattern of אף תכון תבל — the tav is a sign of the bow. And תעור means 'your bow is bared,' and this is like the appearance of the bow that is in the cloud on a day of rain." "And the sense of <b>oaths, rods</b> concerns the arrows; and so it is written: 'the lightning of your spear' (Habakkuk 3:11) — as if the rods swore to fulfill your word, selah." "<b>Rivers, you split the earth</b> — opposite the Name, and the earth, which is the thing split open, is the object acted upon, until it becomes like rivers."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:15.571458112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}